.IX Title "File::Rename::Unicode 3pm"
.TH File::Rename::Unicode 3pm "2023-01-23" "perl v5.36.0" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
File::Rename::Unicode \- Unicode wrapper for user code for File::Rename
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&    require File::Rename::Unicode;
\&    my $sub = File::Rename::Unicode::code($code, $enc);
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SS "\s-1FUNCTIONS\s0"
.IX Subsection "FUNCTIONS"
.ie n .IP """code()""" 4
.el .IP "\f(CWcode()\fR" 4
.IX Item "code()"
Wrap the call to user code in utf8/unicode features.
.SS "\s-1OPTIONS\s0"
.IX Subsection "OPTIONS"
See rename script \-\-unicode option
.PP
See File::Rename for unicode_strings option
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables are used.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBFile::Rename\fR\|(3), \fBrename\fR\|(1)
